{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["And concerning the common people, it says: <b>If one soul sins unwittingly from the people of the land.</b> For this is a nearby possibility — that one of the common people sin. And in this case and in the matter of the ruler's sin, it says 'ואשם,' which is an admonition concerning repentance that precedes the offering. And in both of these and in all guilt-offerings, He assigned a portion to the priests, for the priests' eating effects atonement for the sinners."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:51.678042983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}